---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="MCP server" description="Use NostalgiaUI from Claude Code or Claude Desktop.">
  <h1>MCP server</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    The server exposes NostalgiaUI to any MCP client, so an AI coding agent can ask for the tokens
    and component source it needs rather than guessing.
  </p>

  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Answers</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>list_eras</code></td><td>the eras, with period and label</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>list_palettes</code></td><td>the palettes, with appearance and source licence</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>get_tokens</code></td><td>CSS variables, a Tailwind preset, or DTCG JSON for one pairing</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>get_component</code></td><td>imports, source, era CSS and the traps to avoid</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>import_vscode_theme</code></td><td>a palette from a VS Code theme, with provenance</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>check_contrast</code></td><td>a WCAG audit of one pairing</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Claude Code</h2>
  <p>From a clone of the repo, the included <code>.mcp.json</code> registers the server automatically. From anywhere else:</p>
  <pre><code>claude mcp add --transport stdio nostalgiaui -- node /absolute/path/to/nostalgia-ui/packages/mcp/dist/cli.js</code></pre>

  <h2>Claude Desktop</h2>
  <p>Add the server under <code>mcpServers</code> in <code>claude_desktop_config.json</code>.</p>
  <pre><code>{`{
  "mcpServers": {
    "nostalgiaui": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["/absolute/path/to/nostalgia-ui/packages/mcp/dist/cli.js"]
    }
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Try it</h2>
  <p>
    Ask: <em>build me a settings page in Frutiger Aero with the Nord palette</em>. The agent should
    call <code>get_tokens</code> and <code>get_component</code>, and the notes in each answer tell
    it the things that are easy to get wrong.
  </p>
  <p class="meta">
    The packages are not on npm yet, so build the repo first with <code>pnpm install && pnpm build</code>.
  </p>
</Base>
